+# TASK — codex review: pipeline.82 Employment_Roster derived from Simulation_Ledger
+
+**From:** research-build. **Mode:** read-only adversarial review. No edits, no sheet, no run, no commit.
+**Output:** `docs/for-claude-review/2026-10-17-codex-pipeline82-roster-from-ledger-review.md` — one verdict line per hunt (SHIP / FIX / HOLD) with file:line evidence.
+
+## What changed (commit on main, `scripts/dumpBeatTabs.js` + `scripts/dumpBeatTabs.test.js` + `docs/engine/SHEETS_MANIFEST.md`)
+The sheet tab `Employment_Roster` was a one-shot copy of who-works-where generated 2026-03-01 (`scripts/linkCitizensToEmployers.js`) and never regenerated; by C111 it disagreed with `Simulation_Ledger` on 225 rows (31 different employer, 33 not Active, 51 not on the ledger, 110 employed citizens missing). Readers: `scripts/beatSliceKit.js rosterAtSectors`, `scripts/buildSafetySlice.js:58`, `scripts/buildTransitSlice.js:176`, `scripts/newsroomSourcing.js workplace()/offices` (`:124`, `:193`), `scripts/livedExperiencePacket.js:683` (evidence source string). Builder 2026-10-17: the Simulation_Ledger is the only truth he knows; a second copy should not exist.
+Fix: `dumpBeatTabs.js` no longer reads the tab; `rosterFromLedger(ledgerRaw)` writes `output/beats/Employment_Roster.jsonl` from the Simulation_Ledger read the dump already does (Active rows with a non-blank `EmployerBizId`; `MappingLayer: 'ledger'`; same six keys the readers consume). Dry derivation on the C111 snapshot: 894 rows — 754 same employer as the old tab, 30 corrected, 110 newly present, 85 old rows dropped. Tab deletion is the builder's hand; no script reads it now.
+
+## Hunts
+- **H1 shape contract.** Every reader predicate above still holds on the derived rows (`Status` 'Active' upper-cased compare; `BIZ_ID` join to `Business_Ledger`; `POP_ID`/`CitizenName` truthy). Any reader that keyed on the old `MappingLayer` values (`existing`/`keyword`) or `Status` values `SELF_EMPLOYED`/`UNTRACKED`? grep and say.
+- **H2 the hiring pool.** Blank `EmployerBizId` = the engine's hiring pool (`runCareerEngine.js` engine.135 E3). The derive drops those citizens from the roster instead of inventing SELF_EMPLOYED. Does any slice or sourcing path NEED the old SELF_EMPLOYED rows (Amara Keane, Lucia Polito were `SELF_EMPLOYED` on the tab)? Name the path or confirm none.
+- **H3 prev/ and movement.** The dump's `prev/` carries the old tab-shaped file for one generation; any builder diffs `Employment_Roster` prev vs live (the Transit/Crime delta pattern)? If so, the first derived generation shows a false 225-row "movement".
+- **H4 requireCols.** `EmployerBizId` added to the Simulation_Ledger required columns — the dump now ABORTS if that header is missing. Confirm the live header carries it (snapshot does) and that abort is the right failure (vs. an empty roster).
+- **H5 test integrity.** The seven new assertions in `dumpBeatTabs.test.js` run before `process.exit` and test the derive, not the source text. 25/25 claimed.
+- **H6 who runs the dump.** `dumpBeatTabs.js` is invoked from the run-cycle skill after the Sunday fire (`.claude/skills/run-cycle/SKILL.md:123`), not cron. Confirm there is no other invoker, so the first derived file lands at the C112 dump Sun 2026-10-18 and Monday's 06:15 wakes read it.
